WEBVTT

00:00:03.645 --> 00:00:05.514
(laughs, grunts)

00:00:05.614 --> 00:00:06.881
Move in.

00:00:06.982 --> 00:00:08.450
- AVL!
- Stay where you are!

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:09.685
Move, move, move!

00:00:09.785 --> 00:00:11.453
(grunts, gasps)

00:00:14.356 --> 00:00:15.724
(groans)

00:00:15.824 --> 00:00:18.060
(grunting and groaning)

00:00:19.395 --> 00:00:20.195
(yells)

00:00:20.295 --> 00:00:21.563
- Stay there!
- (electrical crackling)

00:00:21.663 --> 00:00:22.631
(yelps, whimpers)

00:00:22.731 --> 00:00:24.133
Freeze!

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.002
- (weapon blasting)
- (grunting)

00:00:27.102 --> 00:00:30.272
- (whooshing)
- (yells, groans)

00:00:30.372 --> 00:00:31.807
Gotcha.

00:00:31.906 --> 00:00:33.208
No, no, no, no, no, no, no! No!

00:00:33.308 --> 00:00:34.710
- This is not happening.
- (dog whimpering)

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:36.612
<i>C'est impossible.</i> (grunts)

00:00:36.712 --> 00:00:38.313
Get your hands off of me!

00:00:38.414 --> 00:00:40.849
(groans) I...
I am commanding you to let...

00:00:40.948 --> 00:00:42.317
(laughing)

00:00:42.418 --> 00:00:43.752
So long, Maxime.

00:00:43.852 --> 00:00:45.721
Who's the loser now?

00:00:45.821 --> 00:00:46.822
- (blows raspberry)
- Loser!

00:00:46.921 --> 00:00:48.791
BOTH:
Loser! Loser!

00:00:48.891 --> 00:00:51.093
- (Maxime yelling)
- (all gasp)

00:00:52.027 --> 00:00:54.963
- (electrical buzzing)
- (rapid grunting)

00:00:58.567 --> 00:01:00.602
This is not over!

00:01:00.702 --> 00:01:01.936
(all whimpering)

00:01:02.037 --> 00:01:03.839
You won't always have the AVL

00:01:03.938 --> 00:01:05.441
to fight your battles,
you coward.

00:01:05.541 --> 00:01:08.911
Mark my words,
I will exterminate you!

00:01:09.011 --> 00:01:10.312
(Maxime laughing wildly)

00:01:10.412 --> 00:01:12.014
What?

00:01:13.749 --> 00:01:15.684
- (clanking)
- (chuckles)

00:01:15.784 --> 00:01:17.886
Not, uh... not scary at all.

00:01:17.986 --> 00:01:19.721
(laughs nervously)

00:01:19.822 --> 00:01:22.090
♪

00:01:25.527 --> 00:01:27.362
(birds chirping)

00:01:27.463 --> 00:01:29.465
♪

00:01:31.333 --> 00:01:34.203
- (Lucky bleating)
- (Kyle grunting)

00:01:34.937 --> 00:01:36.171
Hello, everybody.

00:01:36.271 --> 00:01:38.040
- EDITH: Gru, what's up?
- AGNES: Hey, Gru!

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:39.975
- Hey, Gru.
- I'm so happy you're here!

00:01:40.075 --> 00:01:42.010
What's shaking in the Gru house?

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:44.179
Look what I taught Lucky.

00:01:44.279 --> 00:01:46.882
- Lucky, sit.
- (bleating)

00:01:46.982 --> 00:01:48.984
(grunts, passes gas)

00:01:49.084 --> 00:01:51.753
Aw, Lucky. I said "sit."

00:01:51.854 --> 00:01:54.289
- (bleats)
- (laughing)

00:01:54.389 --> 00:01:58.160
Well, it is only
his first lesson.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.696
Uh, maybe we practice outside
from now on.

00:02:00.796 --> 00:02:03.165
There's my favorite husband.

00:02:03.265 --> 00:02:05.200
Did you remember
to get the milk?

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:07.202
Well, yes. They had a few kinds.

00:02:07.302 --> 00:02:09.605
They got the almond milk,
soy milk, hemp milk,

00:02:09.705 --> 00:02:12.708
oat milk, goat milk,
chocolate milk, half-and-half,

00:02:12.808 --> 00:02:15.110
powdered and of magnesia.

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:17.279
What about regular milk?

00:02:17.379 --> 00:02:19.648
Uh, they don't make that
anymore.

00:02:19.748 --> 00:02:20.949
Oh.

00:02:21.049 --> 00:02:22.451
Wait a minute.

00:02:22.551 --> 00:02:25.254
- One, two, three girls.
- (Agnes giggling)

00:02:25.354 --> 00:02:26.488
One wife.

00:02:26.588 --> 00:02:29.024
- Something is missing.
- (girls laughing)

00:02:29.124 --> 00:02:32.194
No, I think that's
all of us, yeah.

00:02:32.294 --> 00:02:34.998
You know what,
I keep forgetting-- this guy!

00:02:35.097 --> 00:02:37.799
(laughing, babbling)

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:38.834
(laughing):
Oh!

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:40.003
There's my boy!

00:02:40.135 --> 00:02:42.037
- There he is.
- (cooing)

00:02:42.137 --> 00:02:43.872
A-coochie-coochie-
coochie-coochie.

00:02:43.973 --> 00:02:46.942
Where is Daddy's hug?

00:02:47.042 --> 00:02:49.077
Oh, looks like somebody's
a little cranky.

00:02:49.177 --> 00:02:52.648
- (fussing)
- Behind that sourpuss,

00:02:52.748 --> 00:02:55.183
I know you love your dada!

00:02:55.284 --> 00:02:57.686
Go on, say it. "Dada."

00:02:57.786 --> 00:02:59.221
"Dada."

00:02:59.321 --> 00:03:00.722
- Yes, of course he loves you.
- (laughing)

00:03:00.822 --> 00:03:03.993
He just... he just doesn't
show it on his face.

00:03:04.092 --> 00:03:05.460
Or with his body language.

00:03:05.561 --> 00:03:08.063
(chuckles)
Right, Gru Jr.? Come on.

00:03:08.163 --> 00:03:10.098
Show Daddy
how much you love him.

00:03:10.198 --> 00:03:13.769
Oh, I know what
will make you happy.

00:03:13.869 --> 00:03:16.104
Mmm. Bahama Medley.

00:03:16.204 --> 00:03:18.840
(fusses, squeals)

00:03:18.941 --> 00:03:20.242
No?

00:03:20.342 --> 00:03:22.778
It's from the Bahamas--
all of them.

00:03:22.878 --> 00:03:26.081
Look. Oh, so yummy.

00:03:26.181 --> 00:03:27.416
Mmm, mmm, mmm.

00:03:27.516 --> 00:03:30.118
- (gags, coughs)
- (laughing)

00:03:30.218 --> 00:03:33.056
Oh, that really tastes
like the Bahamas.

00:03:33.155 --> 00:03:35.058
See? He loves his daddy.

00:03:35.157 --> 00:03:37.060
He's sharing. (chuckles)

00:03:37.159 --> 00:03:39.494
(Gru Jr. laughing)

00:03:39.595 --> 00:03:41.064
Phil, Ralph, Ron.

00:03:41.163 --> 00:03:43.398
(Minions grunting rapidly)

00:03:43.498 --> 00:03:46.002
("Hot for Teacher" by Van Halen
playing)

00:03:46.101 --> 00:03:47.235
(speaks Minionese)

00:03:47.336 --> 00:03:48.537
(babbles, speaks Minionese)

00:03:48.637 --> 00:03:50.606
- (laughing)
- (toothbrush buzzing)

00:03:50.706 --> 00:03:52.608
(speaking Minionese)

00:03:56.178 --> 00:03:58.113
- (groans)
- (grunting)

00:03:58.213 --> 00:04:00.349
- (yelps)
- (speaks Minionese)

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:03.518
- (speaking Minionese)
- (drill whirring)

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.288
(speaking Minionese)

00:04:06.388 --> 00:04:08.057
- (song stops)
- (bell dings)

00:04:08.156 --> 00:04:10.592
- Thanks, guys.
- (doorbell rings)

00:04:13.062 --> 00:04:14.262
Ramsbottom?

00:04:14.363 --> 00:04:16.932
- "Bottom."
- (all laughing)

00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:18.900
I need a word with you both.

00:04:19.002 --> 00:04:20.335
- Sure, but what...
- I'm sorry,

00:04:20.435 --> 00:04:21.837
there's no time for chitchat.

00:04:21.937 --> 00:04:25.074
Maxime Le Mal has sent you
a message from prison.

00:04:25.173 --> 00:04:27.076
(static crackling)

00:04:27.175 --> 00:04:28.477
<i>Bonjour, Gru.</i>

00:04:28.577 --> 00:04:30.912
I know you can hear me,
so hear this.

00:04:31.014 --> 00:04:35.183
You think you can humiliate me
and get away with it, yes?

00:04:35.283 --> 00:04:37.419
But no!
When I break out of prison,

00:04:37.519 --> 00:04:39.521
I'm coming for my revenge, Gru,

00:04:39.621 --> 00:04:42.791
but this time,
I won't go so easy on you.

00:04:42.891 --> 00:04:43.993
(laughs)

00:04:44.093 --> 00:04:46.328
And I know where you live,

00:04:46.428 --> 00:04:48.330
so you'd better sleep
with one eye open,

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:51.000
'cause you can't hide from me.
(laughs)

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.701
Sweet dreams, Gru-ser!

00:04:52.801 --> 00:04:53.970
(laughs)

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:55.470
(both gasp)

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:57.706
Don't worry,
he can't get out of there.

00:04:57.806 --> 00:05:00.342
(chuckling):
It's a maximum security prison.

00:05:00.442 --> 00:05:02.277
Ah, yes, well, um...
(clears throat)

00:05:02.377 --> 00:05:04.413
he escaped yesterday.

00:05:04.513 --> 00:05:05.681
What?!

00:05:05.781 --> 00:05:07.182
Leave our home?

00:05:07.282 --> 00:05:08.850
Oh, no, you're gonna love it.

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:10.419
It's-it's called the safe house,

00:05:10.519 --> 00:05:12.320
and it's fun, and it's safe,

00:05:12.421 --> 00:05:14.523
and it's fantastic,
and we're going.

00:05:14.623 --> 00:05:17.093
Yeah, you'll get a new room,
go to a new school.

00:05:17.192 --> 00:05:18.627
That'll be fun, right?

00:05:18.727 --> 00:05:20.195
Everything's gonna be new.
We love new.

00:05:20.295 --> 00:05:22.264
What about all my friends?

00:05:22.364 --> 00:05:24.866
You'll make new friends,
probably better ones.

00:05:24.967 --> 00:05:26.268
(Margo groans)

00:05:26.368 --> 00:05:29.072
- I can't believe this.
- GRU: Yes, yes.

00:05:29.172 --> 00:05:30.872
Lot of emotions,
big life change.

00:05:30.973 --> 00:05:32.307
Less talking, more walking.

00:05:32.407 --> 00:05:34.110
Come on. Here we go.

00:05:34.209 --> 00:05:36.145
♪

00:05:36.244 --> 00:05:38.513
(Minions grunting)

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:42.284
- (Lucky bleats)
- (Margo grunts)

00:05:42.384 --> 00:05:43.585
(Agnes sniffles, whimpers)

00:05:43.685 --> 00:05:46.855
I'm sorry you can't go with us,
Lucky.

00:05:46.956 --> 00:05:48.390
(bleats)

00:05:49.959 --> 00:05:51.827
Take good care of him.

00:05:51.927 --> 00:05:52.894
(bleats)

00:05:52.995 --> 00:05:54.362
Be good, Lucky.

00:05:54.463 --> 00:05:57.967
Don't forget to practice
your tricks.

00:05:58.067 --> 00:06:00.235
- (vehicle door closes)
- (sighs)

00:06:01.903 --> 00:06:04.840
We'll arrive at the AVL
safe house in a few hours.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.942
Mayflower is a lovely town.

00:06:07.043 --> 00:06:09.511
A lovely, safe, boring town.

00:06:09.611 --> 00:06:11.346
Trust me,
it is for the best, Gru.

00:06:11.446 --> 00:06:13.049
And what about Grandma?

00:06:13.149 --> 00:06:14.583
And Uncle Dru?

00:06:14.683 --> 00:06:17.719
I'm sorry, no one can know
of your whereabouts.

00:06:17.819 --> 00:06:18.653
Not even family.

00:06:18.754 --> 00:06:20.789
Bingo,
there's your silver lining.

00:06:20.889 --> 00:06:23.592
And you promise to take care
of the other Minions?

00:06:23.692 --> 00:06:26.828
They'll be safe and sound
at AVL headquarters.

00:06:26.928 --> 00:06:28.998
I have big plans for them.

00:06:29.098 --> 00:06:31.633
(scoffs)
Good luck with that.

00:06:32.334 --> 00:06:35.537
("Boombayah" by Blackpink
playing)

00:06:35.637 --> 00:06:37.439
♪ Been a bad girl, I know I am

00:06:37.539 --> 00:06:39.374
♪ And I'm so hot, I need a fan

00:06:39.474 --> 00:06:41.943
♪ I don't want a boy,
I need a man... ♪

00:06:42.044 --> 00:06:44.546
(Minions laughing, chattering)

00:06:44.646 --> 00:06:47.382
- (noisemakers blaring)
- (whooping)

00:06:50.086 --> 00:06:52.387
(groans)
That is it!

00:06:52.487 --> 00:06:54.856
- (tires squealing)
- (grunting, noisemaker blares)

